humbnail\" alt=\"\" \/><\/a>\n\t\t\t<\/div><\/figure><figure class='gallery-item'>\n\t\t\t<div class='gallery-icon landscape'>\n\t\t\t\t<a href='https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2016\/04\/2016-04-19-13-49-48.jpg'><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"150\" height=\"150\" src=\"https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2016\/04\/2016-04-19-13-49-48-150x150.jpg\" class=\"attachment-thumbnail size-thumbnail\" alt=\"\" \/><\/a>\n\t\t\t<\/div><\/figure><figure class='gallery-item'>\n\t\t\t<div class='gallery-icon landscape'>\n\t\t\t\t<a href='https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2016\/04\/2016-04-19-15-50-35.jpg'><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"150\" height=\"150\" src=\"https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2016\/04\/2016-04-19-15-50-35-150x150.jpg\" class=\"attachment-thumbnail size-thumbnail\" alt=\"\" \/><\/a>\n\t\t\t<\/div><\/figure><figure class='gallery-item'>\n\t\t\t<div class='gallery-icon landscape'>\n\t\t\t\t<a href='https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2016\/04\/2016-04-19-14-47-49.jpg'><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"150\" height=\"150\" src=\"https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2016\/04\/2016-04-19-14-47-49-150x150.jpg\" class=\"attachment-thumbnail size-thumbnail\" alt=\"\" \/><\/a>\n\t\t\t<\/div><\/figure><figure class='gallery-item'>\n\t\t\t<div class='gallery-icon landscape'>\n\t\t\t\t<a href='https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2016\/04\/2016-04-19-13-06-58.jpg'><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"150\" height=\"150\" src=\"https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2016\/04\/2016-04-19-13-06-58-150x150.jpg\" class=\"attachment-thumbnail size-thumbnail\" alt=\"\" \/><\/a>\n\t\t\t<\/div><\/figure>\n\t\t<\/div>\n\n<p><strong>NOTE<\/strong>: We WILL be back here at some time and on that visit we will board the train in Williams that departs the station at 9:30 am, then gets up to the Grand Canyon about noon. \u00a0Up there you then hop on a park shuttle bus that takes you around all the sites, returning to the departing train about 3pm and back at Williams by about 5:30. \u00a0This, I think, would be a more laid back relaxing way of seeing not only the canyon, but also all the magnificent terrain on the way up, (when you&#8217;re driving you need to keep your eye on the double yellow line!)<\/p>\n","protected":false},"excerpt":{"rendered":"<p>We certainly couldn&#8217;t spend any time in the Grand Canyon state without taking a trip up there now could we? So Tuesday morning we headed out about 9 o&#8217;clock and soon found out it&#8217;s a lot further &#8220;up the road&#8221; than it looked on the map. \u00a0We stoppped along the way at the little town &hellip; <a href=\"https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/2016\/04\/23\/tuesday-to-the-grand-canyon\/\" class=\"more-link\">Continue reading <span class=\"screen-reader-text\">Tuesday to the Grand Canyon<\/span><\/a><\/p>\n","protected":false},"author":1,"featured_media":0,"comment_status":"open","ping_status":"open","sticky":false,"template":"","format":"standard","meta":{"footnotes":""},"categories":[19546],"tags":[179795,79934,15573],"class_list":["post-824","post","type-post","status-publish","format-standard","hentry","category-sightseeing","tag-grand-canyon","tag-train","tag-williams"],"_links":{"self":[{"href":"https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/posts\/824","targetHints":{"allow":["GET"]}}],"collection":[{"href":"https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/posts"}],"about":[{"href":"https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/types\/post"}],"author":[{"embeddable":true,"href":"https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/users\/1"}],"replies":[{"embeddable":true,"href":"https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/comments?post=824"}],"version-history":[{"count":16,"href":"https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/posts\/824\/revisions"}],"predecessor-version":[{"id":931,"href":"https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/posts\/824\/revisio